{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>For an astonishment.</b> Like תִּמָּהוֹן; אש״ו אשטורדישו״ן — everyone who sees you will be astonished over you." "<b>For a proverb.</b> When a bad calamity comes upon a person, they say: this is like the calamity of so-and-so." "<b>And for a taunt.</b> From the root of ״וְשִׁנַּנְתָּם״ (Deuteronomy 6) — they will speak of you. And so its Targum: וּלְשׁוֹעֵי — a term of telling and recounting."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {0 "the la'az אש״ו אשטורדישו״ן is Old French es toi (à toi) estordison, 'an astonishment upon you'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:48:40.434904472Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}